      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t have a flag to indicate that we sent a chunk request, or actually any message that we are pending on a tx message to be complete. There are places where we wait for the transmit done flag, but we don\u0027t have a flag to indicate we expect a transmit message to complete. The PRL_FLAGS_MSG_XMIT flag get\u0027s cleared before we send a message, as that\u0027s relative to the PE layer.\n\nI think my thought here was that getting an rx message once in this state is an expected outcome. The flag PRL_FLAGS_TX_COMPLETE won\u0027t be set until the prl_tx state machine can run. My thought was that advancing to rch_waiting_chunk_run doesn\u0027t lead to anything else unless a message is received. It would time out anyway.",
